From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:17:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: don't re-enter tx_lock from the SSR
 teardown

An ADSP subsystem restart deadlocks the SoC. qcom_slim_ngd_ssr_pdr_notify()
takes tx_lock and, still holding it, calls qcom_slim_ngd_down(), which
reports every child device absent. On a board whose codec is an MFD
parent - a WCD934X on a Pixel 2 XL - that removal reaches the children's
free_irq(), regmap-irq flushes the interrupt masks back out over
SLIMbus, and the write lands in qcom_slim_ngd_xfer_msg() on the very
thread that already holds tx_lock. Nothing recovers: hung-task detection
panics the machine some 30 seconds later, which on a phone reads as an
unexplained hard hang rather than as a lockup.

Refuse transfers for the duration of the teardown, before touching the
lock. The bus is already gone by then, so the writes could not have
landed anyway and failing them fast is what breaks the cycle.

The flag is deliberately not the controller state: that is DOWN for the
whole of bring-up too, and refusing there breaks enumeration - the
logical address lookup fails and the sound card never appears.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index cd40ab839c54..cd01782a9db1 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -168,6 +168,8 @@ struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl {
 	void *notifier;
 	struct pdr_handle *pdr;
 	enum qcom_slim_ngd_state state;
+	/* set only while the SSR notifier tears the children down under tx_lock */
+	bool ssr_teardown;
 	dma_addr_t rx_phys_base;
 	dma_addr_t tx_phys_base;
 	void *rx_base;
@@ -797,6 +799,30 @@ static int qcom_slim_ngd_xfer_msg(struct slim_controller *sctrl,
 	u8 la = txn->la;
 	bool usr_msg = false;
 
+	/*
+	 * Refuse transfers issued from inside the SSR teardown, before touching
+	 * tx_lock.
+	 *
+	 * qcom_slim_ngd_ssr_pdr_notify() takes tx_lock and, still holding it,
+	 * calls qcom_slim_ngd_down() -> slim_report_absent() for every child.
+	 * A codec driver removing its own children from there makes their
+	 * free_irq() flush the interrupt masks back out over SLIMbus, i.e.
+	 * straight back into this function. Taking tx_lock again from the
+	 * thread that already holds it deadlocks the teardown for good, and
+	 * hung-task detection then takes the machine down some 30 seconds
+	 * later. The bus is gone by that point, so failing fast costs nothing.
+	 *
+	 * This is keyed on the teardown flag rather than on the DOWN state
+	 * because the state is also DOWN for the whole of bring-up, where
+	 * refusing transfers would break enumeration.
+	 */
+	if (ctrl->ssr_teardown) {
+		dev_err_ratelimited(ctrl->dev,
+				    "SSR teardown, refusing xfer mc:0x%x mt:0x%x\n",
+				    txn->mc, txn->mt);
+		return -ENOTCONN;
+	}
+
 	if (txn->mt == SLIM_MSG_MT_CORE &&
 		(txn->mc >= SLIM_MSG_MC_BEGIN_RECONFIGURATION &&
 		 txn->mc <= SLIM_MSG_MC_RECONFIGURE_NOW))
@@ -1476,8 +1502,15 @@ static int qcom_slim_ngd_ssr_pdr_notify(struct qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl *ctrl,
 		if (ctrl->state != QCOM_SLIM_NGD_CTRL_DOWN) {
 			pm_runtime_get_noresume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
 			ctrl->state = QCOM_SLIM_NGD_CTRL_DOWN;
+			/*
+			 * Everything up to the reset below runs with tx_lock
+			 * held and can re-enter xfer_msg through the children's
+			 * teardown; see the comment there.
+			 */
+			ctrl->ssr_teardown = true;
 			qcom_slim_ngd_down(ctrl);
 			qcom_slim_ngd_exit_dma(ctrl);
+			ctrl->ssr_teardown = false;
 		}
 		mutex_unlock(&ctrl->tx_lock);
 		break;
